  </address>

  <h2 id="hosting">Hosting and server logs</h2>
  <p>
    evicons.dev is a static website. It is served from a server in Germany that the controller operates himself. On
    every request the web server stores an access log with the IP address, the time, the requested address (URL) and
    the user agent (browser and operating system). These data are processed for the security and operation of the
    website, for example to detect errors and attacks, and are deleted after 14 days at the latest.
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. The legitimate interest lies in the secure and stable operation of the
    website.
  </p>
  <p>This website does not set cookies.</p>

  <h2 id="statistics">Statistics (OpenPanel)</h2>
  <p>
    To understand which icons and which parts of the documentation are used, we keep cookieless statistics with
    OpenPanel. We run OpenPanel ourselves on our own server in Germany, and evicons.dev serves the statistics script
    itself. We record the page visited, the referring page, the browser, operating system, device type and the
    approximate origin (country, region), as well as single actions such as copying a code example, downloading an icon
    or following a link to another website, and the terms searched in the icon gallery (shortened to 40 characters)
    with the number of icons they found.
  </p>
  <p>
    The measurements reach OpenPanel through our web server. Before that, we shorten your IP address (IPv4: last block
    set to 0, IPv6: only the first three blocks kept), so that it can no longer be linked to a single connection; only
    the shortened address is stored. No cookies are set, no profiles across devices or websites are built and no data
    are passed on to third parties. The statistics are stored until we delete them, for 24 months at most.
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. The legitimate interest lies in privacy-friendly statistics that help us
    develop the library and its documentation according to actual needs. You can object to this processing (see
    <a href="#rights">Your rights</a>).
  </p>

  <h2 id="local-storage">Local storage</h2>
  <p>
    If you choose the light or dark colour scheme with the switch in the header, your browser stores this choice in its
    local storage (localStorage). The entry contains no personal data, stays on your device and is not sent to the
    server or to third parties. Storing it is necessary for the function you chose (Section 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG). You can
    delete the entry at any time in your browser settings.
  </p>

  <h2 id="map-tiles">Map tiles on /map</h2>
  <p>
    Only the <a href="/map">Map</a> page shows a map. When you open it, your browser loads the map tiles and the map
    style from OpenFreeMap (tiles.openfreemap.org), operated by Hyperknot Software Kft., Hungary (EU). Your IP address is
    sent to this provider, because the tiles cannot be delivered to your browser otherwise.
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. The legitimate interest lies in showing the library's map markers on a real
    map. No map tiles are loaded on any other page. For details, see the
    <a href="https://openfreemap.org/privacy/">OpenFreeMap privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="external-links">External links</h2>
  <p>
    This website links to external services, for example GitHub and npm. Merely visiting this website sends no data to
    these providers. Only when you follow a link does the privacy policy of the respective provider apply.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
  <p>You have the right, with respect to the controller, to</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access to the data processed about you (Art. 15 GDPR),</li>
    <li>rectification of inaccurate data (Art. 16 GDPR),</li>
    <li>erasure (Art. 17 GDPR),</li>
    <li>restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR),</li>
    <li>object to processing based on Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (Art. 21 GDPR).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise them, contact <a href="mailto:abdellatif@landolsi.de">abdellatif@landolsi.de</a>. You can also lodge a
    complaint with a data protection supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR). The competent authority is the Bavarian State
    Office for Data Protection Supervision (Bayerisches Landesamt für Datenschutzaufsicht, BayLDA), Promenade 18, 91522
    Ansbach, Germany, <a href="https://www.lda.bayern.de">www.lda.bayern.de</a>.
  </p>

  <p class="legal-date">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-11-25">25 November 2026</time></p>
</Legal>
